module

public import TauCeti.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Tower.Ring
public import TauCeti.Algebra.Lie.Current.LeftIdeal

/-!
# The completed enveloping algebra of a residue central extension at a fixed level

Let `ĝ = L((t)) ⊕ R K` be the residue central extension of an invariant symmetric form `Φ`, let
`U = U(ĝ) / (ι K - a)` be its enveloping algebra at the central value `a`
(`TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.CentralQuotient`), and let `I_N = U · ι(a_N)` be the left ideal
generated by the currents of order at least `N` (`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.orderLeftIdeal`). The
completed enveloping algebra is the inverse limit

`Û = lim_N U / I_N`

of the discrete left `U`-modules `Q_N = U / I_N`, that is the module of compatible families of
classes. This file defines it as the limit of the tower of quotients `Q_0 ← Q_1 ← Q_2 ← ⋯`
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.orderQuotientTower`), indexed by the natural numbers, which are cofinal
among the orders. At `a = 1` and `Φ = -κ` it is the completion `Û_κ` of the level enveloping
algebra.

The completion is an `R`-algebra. Its multiplication is `(x y)_N = x · y_N`, where `x` acts on the
smooth `U`-module `Q_N` by the extension `TauCeti.ModuleTower.limSmul` of the action of `U`
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.limπ_mul`); this is the construction `TauCeti.ModuleTower.limRing` of
`TauCeti.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Tower.Ring`, which applies because of the right-shift estimate
`I_M b ⊆ I_N`. The canonical map `U → Û` is an algebra map
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.toCompletedEnveloping`), and the action of `U` on `Û` is left
multiplication by its image. The kernels of the projections `Û → Q_N` are open and closed left
ideals of `Û` (`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.completedOrderLeftIdeal`), not two-sided ones, and they
satisfy the right-shift estimate again: for every `y ∈ Û` and every `N` there is `M` with
`ker π_M · y ⊆ ker π_N`. Hence `Û` is a topological ring with a left-linear topology.

The completion carries the inverse limit topology of
`TauCeti.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Tower.Topology`: the kernels of the projections `Û → Q_N`
form a basis of neighbourhoods of zero, and it is Hausdorff and complete. The canonical map
`U → Û` (`TauCeti.ModuleTower.toLimQuotients`) has dense range, induces on `U` the linear topology
defined by the `I_N`, and has kernel the intersection of all `I_N`
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.ker_toLimQuotients_orderLeftIdeal`).

The action of `U` on `Û` has continuous orbit maps for the `I`-topology on `U`: for every `x ∈ Û`
and every `N` there is `M` such that `I_M x` lies in the kernel of the projection to `Q_N`
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.exists_forall_limπ_smul_eq_zero`). This is the right-shift estimate
`I_M b ⊆ I_N` applied to a representative `b` of the `N`-th coordinate of `x`.

**Functoriality.** An algebra morphism `g : U(ĝ_Ψ) / (ι K - b) → U(ĝ_Φ) / (ι K - a)` between
enveloping algebras of residue extensions of the same Lie algebra which is continuous for the
topologies of the left ideals, in that for every `n` it carries the currents of some order `m` into
`I_n`, extends uniquely to a continuous algebra morphism of the completions
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.completedEnvelopingMap`), compatibly with identities and composition.
Continuity only needs to be checked on generators, since `I_m` is the left ideal generated by the
currents of order at least `m`. An algebra isomorphism `e` with `e` and `e⁻¹` continuous in
this sense extends to an algebra isomorphism of the completions which is a homeomorphism
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.completedEnvelopingEquiv`).

**The completed level comparison.** If `Ψ = k • Φ`, the level comparison
`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.levelEnvelopingEquiv` from `U(ĝ_Ψ) / (ι K - 1)` to `U(ĝ_Φ) / (ι K - k)` is
the identity on currents, so it and its inverse carry each `I_n` onto `I_n`. It therefore extends
to an algebra isomorphism and homeomorphism of the completions which matches the kernels of the
projections to `U / I_n` (`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.levelCompletedEnvelopingEquiv`), for every `k`,
including `k = 0`. Thus the completion `Û_κ` of the level enveloping algebra of `κ = k κ₀` is the
completion of `U(ĝ_κ₀) / (K - k)`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.orderQuotientTower`: the tower of the quotients `U / I_n`.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.CompletedEnveloping`: the completed enveloping algebra `lim_n U / I_n`,
  with its instances of `Ring`, `Algebra R`, `IsTopologicalRing` and left `IsLinearTopology`.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.toCompletedEnveloping`: the canonical algebra map `U → Û`.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.completedOrderLeftIdeal`: the kernel of the projection `Û → U / I_n`, as
  a left ideal of `Û`.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.completedEnvelopingMap`: the extension of a continuous algebra morphism
  to the completions.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.completedEnvelopingEquiv`: the extension of an algebra isomorphism which
  is continuous in both directions.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.levelCompletedEnvelopingEquiv`: the completed level comparison.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.ker_toLimQuotients_orderLeftIdeal`: the kernel of `U → Û` is the
  intersection of the `I_N`.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.exists_forall_limπ_smul_eq_zero`: the orbit maps of the action of `U` on
  `Û` are continuous.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.limπ_mul`: the coordinates of a product, `(x y)_N = x · y_N`.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.mul_limSmul`, `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.one_limSmul`: on a smooth module,
  `(x y) · m = x · (y · m)` and `1 · m = m`.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.limSmul_toCompletedEnveloping`: on a smooth module, the image in `Û` of
  `b ∈ U` acts as `b`.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.limπ_one`, `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.coe_one_apply`: the coordinates of
  the unit are the classes of `1`.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.limπ_toCompletedEnveloping`: the coordinates of the image of `b ∈ U` are
  the classes of `b`.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.exists_forall_mul_mem_completedOrderLeftIdeal`: the right-shift estimate
  in `Û`.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.eq_completedEnvelopingMap`: uniqueness of continuous extensions.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.levelCompletedEnvelopingEquiv_mem_completedOrderLeftIdeal_iff`: the
  completed level comparison matches the kernels of the projections to `U / I_n`.

## References

* E. Frenkel, *Langlands Correspondence for Loop Groups*, §2.1.2 and §3.2.1, for the completion
  `lim_N U / I_N` of the enveloping algebra of an affine Kac--Moody algebra at a fixed level.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra Topology
open LieAlgebra.ofTwoCocycle (centralElement envelopingι)

namespace TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra

variable {R L : Type*} [CommRing R] [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra R L]

section Completion

variable (Φ : LinearMap.BilinForm R L) (hΦ : Φ.lieInvariant L) (hΦs : Φ.IsSymm) (a : R)

local notation "UK" => CentralQuotient R (centralElement (twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Φ hΦ hΦs)) a

/-- The tower `U / I_0 ← U / I_1 ← U / I_2 ← ⋯` of the quotients of `U(ĝ) / (ι K - a)` by the left
ideals of high-order currents, with the quotient maps as transitions. -/
abbrev orderQuotientTower : ModuleTower UK :=
  ModuleTower.quotients _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs a)

/-- **The completed enveloping algebra** `Û = lim_n U / I_n` of the residue central extension of
`Φ` at the central value `a`: the left `U`-module of compatible families of classes modulo the left
ideals of high-order currents, with the inverse limit topology. -/
abbrev CompletedEnveloping : Type _ :=
  (orderQuotientTower Φ hΦ hΦs a).lim

/-- **The kernel of the canonical map** `U → Û` is the intersection of all the left ideals `I_N`.
In particular `U` embeds in its completion exactly when the `I_N` intersect to zero. -/
theorem ker_toLimQuotients_orderLeftIdeal :
    LinearMap.ker (ModuleTower.toLimQuotients _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs a)) =
      ⨅ N : ℤ, orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a N := by
  rw [ModuleTower.ker_toLimQuotients, iInf_orderLeftIdeal_natCast]

variable {Φ hΦ hΦs a} in
/-- **The orbit maps of `U` on its completion are continuous.** For every `x ∈ Û` and every `n`
there is an order `M` such that every element of `I_M` moves `x` into the kernel of the projection
`Û → U / I_n`. -/
theorem exists_forall_limπ_smul_eq_zero (x : CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) (n : ℕ) :
    ∃ M : ℤ, ∀ b ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a M,
      (orderQuotientTower Φ hΦ hΦs a).limπ n (b • x) = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := ModuleTower.quotientsπ_surjective _ _ n
    ((orderQuotientTower Φ hΦ hΦs a).limπ n x)
  obtain ⟨M, hM⟩ := exists_forall_mul_mem_orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a c n
  refine ⟨M, fun b hb ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [map_smul, ← hc, ← map_smul, smul_eq_mul, ModuleTower.quotientsπ_eq_zero_iff]
  exact hM b hb

/-! ### The ring structure -/

/-- **The completed enveloping algebra is a ring**, with `(x y)_n = x · y_n` for the action of `Û`
on the smooth module `U / I_n` extending that of `U`, and unit the image of `1`. -/
instance : Ring (CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) :=
  ModuleTower.limRing (exists_forall_mul_mem_orderLeftIdeal_natCast Φ hΦ hΦs a)

variable {Φ hΦ hΦs a}

/-- The coordinates of a product in the completed enveloping algebra: `(x y)_n = x · y_n`, where
`x` acts on the smooth module `U / I_n` as any representative of its `n`-th coordinate. -/
theorem limπ_mul (x y : CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) (n : ℕ) :
    (orderQuotientTower Φ hΦ hΦs a).limπ n (x * y) =
      ModuleTower.limSmul
        (ModuleTower.smoothModules_quotients_obj
          (exists_forall_mul_mem_orderLeftIdeal_natCast Φ hΦ hΦs a) n)
        x ((orderQuotientTower Φ hΦ hΦs a).limπ n y) :=
  ModuleTower.limπ_limMul _ x y n

/-- The action of a product on a smooth module is the composite of the actions,
`(x y) • m = x • (y • m)`, for the extension `TauCeti.ModuleTower.limSmul` of the action of `U`. -/
theorem mul_limSmul {M : ModuleCat UK}
    (hM : smoothModules (fun n : ℕ ↦ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n) M)
    (x y : CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) (m : M) :
    ModuleTower.limSmul hM (x * y) m = ModuleTower.limSmul hM x (ModuleTower.limSmul hM y m) :=
  ModuleTower.limSmul_limMul _ hM x y m

/-- The coordinates of the unit of the completed enveloping algebra: `1_n` is the class of `1`. -/
theorem limπ_one (n : ℕ) :
    (orderQuotientTower Φ hΦ hΦs a).limπ n 1 =
      ModuleTower.quotientsπ _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs a) n 1 :=
  LinearMap.congr_fun (ModuleTower.limπ_comp_toLimQuotients _ _ n) 1

/-- The coordinates of the unit of the completed enveloping algebra, in the simp normal form
`↑x n` of `TauCeti.ModuleTower.limπ_apply`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_one_apply (n : ℕ) :
    ((1 : CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) : (orderQuotientTower Φ hΦ hΦs a).Product) n =
      ModuleTower.quotientsπ _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs a) n 1 :=
  (ModuleTower.limπ_apply _ n 1).symm.trans (limπ_one n)

variable (Φ hΦ hΦs a)

/-- The completed enveloping algebra is an `R`-algebra, through the canonical map `U → Û`. Its
scalar multiplication by `r : R` is the action of the image of `r` in `U`. -/
instance : Algebra R (CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) where
  smul r x := algebraMap R UK r • x
  -- The unit of `Û` is the image of `1` and its multiplication is `ModuleTower.limMul`.
  algebraMap :=
    { toFun r := ModuleTower.toLimQuotients _ _ (algebraMap R UK r)
      map_one' := congrArg (ModuleTower.toLimQuotients _ _) (map_one _)
      map_mul' r s := (congrArg (ModuleTower.toLimQuotients _ _) (map_mul _ r s)).trans
        (ModuleTower.toLimQuotients_mul (exists_forall_mul_mem_orderLeftIdeal_natCast Φ hΦ hΦs a)
          _ _)
      map_zero' := by rw [map_zero, map_zero]
      map_add' r s := by rw [map_add, map_add] }
  commutes' r x := (ModuleTower.smul_eq_limMul _ _ x).symm.trans
    (ModuleTower.limMul_toLimQuotients_of_commute _ (fun b ↦ Algebra.commute_algebraMap_right r b)
      x).symm
  smul_def' r x := ModuleTower.smul_eq_limMul _ _ x

instance : IsScalarTower R UK (CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) :=
  .of_algebraMap_smul fun _ _ ↦ rfl

/-- **The canonical algebra map** `U → Û` from the enveloping algebra at a fixed level to its
completion, sending an element to the family of its classes modulo the left ideals `I_n`. -/
def toCompletedEnveloping : UK →ₐ[R] CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a :=
  { ModuleTower.toLimRingHom (exists_forall_mul_mem_orderLeftIdeal_natCast Φ hΦ hΦs a) with
    commutes' r := congrFun (ModuleTower.coe_toLimRingHom _) (algebraMap R UK r) }

@[simp]
theorem coe_toCompletedEnveloping :
    ⇑(toCompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) =
      ModuleTower.toLimQuotients _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs a) :=
  ModuleTower.coe_toLimRingHom _

/-- The canonical algebra map `U → Û` is the canonical ring homomorphism
`TauCeti.ModuleTower.toLimRingHom` into the completion. -/
@[simp]
theorem toRingHom_toCompletedEnveloping :
    (toCompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a : UK →+* CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) =
      ModuleTower.toLimRingHom (exists_forall_mul_mem_orderLeftIdeal_natCast Φ hΦ hΦs a) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The canonical map from the enveloping algebra to its completion has dense range. -/
theorem denseRange_toCompletedEnveloping : DenseRange (toCompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) := by
  simpa only [coe_toCompletedEnveloping] using
    (ModuleTower.denseRange_toLimQuotients _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs a))

variable {Φ hΦ hΦs a}

/-- The action of `U` on its completion is left multiplication by the canonical image. -/
theorem smul_eq_toCompletedEnveloping_mul (b : UK) (x : CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) :
    b • x = toCompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a b * x := by
  rw [coe_toCompletedEnveloping]
  exact ModuleTower.smul_eq_limMul _ b x

/-- The coordinate in `U / I_n` of the image of `b ∈ U` in the completion is the class of `b`. -/
theorem limπ_toCompletedEnveloping (n : ℕ) (b : UK) :
    (orderQuotientTower Φ hΦ hΦs a).limπ n (toCompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a b) =
      ModuleTower.quotientsπ _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs a) n b := by
  rw [coe_toCompletedEnveloping, ← LinearMap.comp_apply, ModuleTower.limπ_comp_toLimQuotients]

/-- On a smooth module, the image in `Û` of an element of `U` acts as that element. -/
theorem limSmul_toCompletedEnveloping {M : ModuleCat UK}
    (hM : smoothModules (fun n : ℕ ↦ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n) M) (b : UK) (m : M) :
    ModuleTower.limSmul hM (toCompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a b) m = b • m := by
  rw [coe_toCompletedEnveloping]
  exact ModuleTower.limSmul_toLimQuotients hM b m

/-- The unit of the completed enveloping algebra acts trivially on a smooth module. -/
@[simp]
theorem one_limSmul {M : ModuleCat UK}
    (hM : smoothModules (fun n : ℕ ↦ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n) M) (m : M) :
    ModuleTower.limSmul hM (1 : CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) m = m := by
  rw [← map_one (toCompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a), limSmul_toCompletedEnveloping, one_smul]

variable (Φ hΦ hΦs a)

/-- **The kernel of the projection** `Û → U / I_n`, a left ideal of the completed enveloping
algebra. -/
def completedOrderLeftIdeal (n : ℕ) :
    Submodule (CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) (CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) where
  carrier := LinearMap.ker ((orderQuotientTower Φ hΦ hΦs a).limπ n)
  add_mem' := add_mem
  zero_mem' := zero_mem _
  smul_mem' x _ hy := ModuleTower.limπ_limMul_eq_zero _ x hy

variable {Φ hΦ hΦs a}

@[simp]
theorem mem_completedOrderLeftIdeal {n : ℕ} {x : CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a} :
    x ∈ completedOrderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n ↔ (orderQuotientTower Φ hΦ hΦs a).limπ n x = 0 :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- The canonical image lies in a stage kernel exactly when the original element lies in
that stage's current-order left ideal. -/
theorem toCompletedEnveloping_mem_completedOrderLeftIdeal_iff {n : ℕ} {b : UK} :
    toCompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a b ∈ completedOrderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n ↔
      b ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n := by
  simp only [coe_toCompletedEnveloping, mem_completedOrderLeftIdeal, ModuleTower.limπ_apply,
    ModuleTower.coe_toLimQuotients_apply, ModuleTower.quotientsπ_eq_zero_iff]

/-- **The right-shift estimate in the completed enveloping algebra.** For every `y ∈ Û` and every
`n` there is `m` such that `x y` lies in the kernel of the projection to `U / I_n` whenever `x` lies
in that of the projection to `U / I_m`. -/
theorem exists_forall_mul_mem_completedOrderLeftIdeal (y : CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a)
    (n : ℕ) : ∃ m, ∀ x ∈ completedOrderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a m,
      x * y ∈ completedOrderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n :=
  ModuleTower.exists_forall_limπ_limMul_eq_zero _ y n

variable (Φ hΦ hΦs a)

/-- The left ideals `ker (Û → U / I_n)` form a basis of neighbourhoods of zero. -/
theorem hasBasis_nhds_zero_completedOrderLeftIdeal :
    (𝓝 (0 : CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a)).HasBasis (fun _ : ℕ ↦ True)
      fun n ↦ (completedOrderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n : Set (CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a)) :=
  (orderQuotientTower Φ hΦ hΦs a).hasBasis_nhds_zero

/-- The topology of the completed enveloping algebra is linear for its left ideals. -/
instance : IsLinearTopology (CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) (CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) :=
  .mk_of_hasBasis _ (hasBasis_nhds_zero_completedOrderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a)

/-- Multiplication on the completed enveloping algebra is continuous. -/
instance : IsTopologicalRing (CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) where
  continuous_mul := ModuleTower.continuous_limMul _

/-- The left ideals `ker (Û → U / I_n)` are closed. -/
theorem isClosed_completedOrderLeftIdeal (n : ℕ) :
    IsClosed (completedOrderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n : Set (CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a)) :=
  (orderQuotientTower Φ hΦ hΦs a).isClosed_ker_limπ n

/-- The left ideals `ker (Û → U / I_n)` are open. -/
theorem isOpen_completedOrderLeftIdeal (n : ℕ) :
    IsOpen (completedOrderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n : Set (CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a)) :=
  (orderQuotientTower Φ hΦ hΦs a).isOpen_ker_limπ n

end Completion

/-! ### Functoriality -/

section Map

variable {Φ Ψ Θ : LinearMap.BilinForm R L} {hΦ : Φ.lieInvariant L} {hΦs : Φ.IsSymm}
  {hΨ : Ψ.lieInvariant L} {hΨs : Ψ.IsSymm} {hΘ : Θ.lieInvariant L} {hΘs : Θ.IsSymm} {a b c : R}

local notation "cΦ" => twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Φ hΦ hΦs
local notation "cΨ" => twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Ψ hΨ hΨs
local notation "cΘ" => twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Θ hΘ hΘs
local notation "UΨ" => CentralQuotient R (centralElement cΨ) b
local notation "UΦ" => CentralQuotient R (centralElement cΦ) a

/-- An algebra morphism which carries, for every `n`, the currents of some order `m` into `I_n`
carries, for every `n`, some `I_m` into `I_n`. -/
private theorem exists_orderLeftIdeal_le_comap {g : UΨ →ₐ[R] UΦ}
    (hg : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ m : ℕ, ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L m,
      g (envelopingι cΨ b u) ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n) (n : ℕ) :
    ∃ m : ℕ, orderLeftIdeal Ψ hΨ hΨs b m ≤
      (orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n).comap g.toRingHom.toSemilinearMap := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := hg n
  exact ⟨m, fun x hx ↦ orderLeftIdeal_le_comap hm hx⟩

/-- **Functoriality of the completed enveloping algebra.** An algebra morphism
`g : U(ĝ_Ψ) / (ι K - b) → U(ĝ_Φ) / (ι K - a)` which is continuous for the topologies of the left
ideals `I_N`, in that for every `n` it carries the currents of some order `m` into `I_n`, extends
to an algebra morphism of the completions `lim_N U / I_N`. It is continuous
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.continuous_completedEnvelopingMap`), and it is the only continuous
extension of `g` (`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.eq_completedEnvelopingMap`). -/
def completedEnvelopingMap (g : UΨ →ₐ[R] UΦ)
    (hg : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ m : ℕ, ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L m,
      g (envelopingι cΨ b u) ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n) :
    CompletedEnveloping Ψ hΨ hΨs b →ₐ[R] CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a where
  toFun := ModuleTower.limQuotientsMap _ _ g.toRingHom.toSemilinearMap
    (exists_orderLeftIdeal_le_comap hg)
  map_one' := by
    rw [← map_one (toCompletedEnveloping Ψ hΨ hΨs b), ← map_one (toCompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a),
      coe_toCompletedEnveloping, coe_toCompletedEnveloping,
      ModuleTower.limQuotientsMap_toLimQuotients, RingHom.coe_toSemilinearMap, map_one]
  map_mul' := ModuleTower.limQuotientsMap_limMul _ _ _ _ _
  map_zero' := map_zero _
  map_add' := map_add _
  commutes' r := by
    rw [← (toCompletedEnveloping Ψ hΨ hΨs b).commutes,
      ← (toCompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a).commutes, coe_toCompletedEnveloping,
      coe_toCompletedEnveloping, ModuleTower.limQuotientsMap_toLimQuotients,
      RingHom.coe_toSemilinearMap]
    exact congrArg _ (g.commutes r)

variable (g : CentralQuotient R (centralElement (twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Ψ hΨ hΨs)) b →ₐ[R]
    CentralQuotient R (centralElement (twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Φ hΦ hΦs)) a)
  (hg : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ m : ℕ, ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L m,
    g (envelopingι (twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Ψ hΨ hΨs) b u) ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n)

/-- The extension of `g` to the completions extends `g`, along the canonical maps `U → Û`
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.toCompletedEnveloping`, in the simp normal form
`TauCeti.ModuleTower.toLimQuotients`). -/
@[simp]
theorem completedEnvelopingMap_toLimQuotients (x : UΨ) :
    completedEnvelopingMap g hg
        (ModuleTower.toLimQuotients _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Ψ hΨ hΨs b) x) =
      ModuleTower.toLimQuotients _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs a) (g x) :=
  ModuleTower.limQuotientsMap_toLimQuotients _ _ _ _ x

/-- The coordinates of the extension of `g`: if `g` carries the currents of order `m` into `I_n`,
the `n`-th coordinate of the image of `x` is the class of `g y` for any representative `y` of the
`m`-th coordinate of `x`. -/
theorem limπ_completedEnvelopingMap {x : CompletedEnveloping Ψ hΨ hΨs b} {n m : ℕ}
    (hm : ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L m, g (envelopingι cΨ b u) ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n)
    {y : UΨ} (hy : ModuleTower.quotientsπ _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Ψ hΨ hΨs b) m y =
      (orderQuotientTower Ψ hΨ hΨs b).limπ m x) :
    (orderQuotientTower Φ hΦ hΦs a).limπ n (completedEnvelopingMap g hg x) =
      ModuleTower.quotientsπ _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs a) n (g y) :=
  ModuleTower.limπ_limQuotientsMap _ _ _ _ (fun _ hz ↦ orderLeftIdeal_le_comap hm hz) hy

/-- If `g` carries the currents of order `m` into `I_n`, its extension carries the kernel of the
projection to `U / I_m` into the kernel of the projection to `U / I_n`. -/
theorem completedEnvelopingMap_mem_completedOrderLeftIdeal {n m : ℕ}
    (hm : ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L m, g (envelopingι cΨ b u) ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n)
    {x : CompletedEnveloping Ψ hΨ hΨs b} (hx : x ∈ completedOrderLeftIdeal Ψ hΨ hΨs b m) :
    completedEnvelopingMap g hg x ∈ completedOrderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n := by
  rw [mem_completedOrderLeftIdeal] at hx ⊢
  rw [limπ_completedEnvelopingMap g hg hm (y := 0) (by rw [map_zero, hx]), map_zero, map_zero]

/-- The extension of `g` to the completions is continuous. -/
theorem continuous_completedEnvelopingMap : Continuous (completedEnvelopingMap g hg) :=
  ModuleTower.continuous_limQuotientsMap _ _ _ _

/-- **Uniqueness of the extension.** A continuous algebra morphism of completions which extends
`g` is `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.completedEnvelopingMap g hg`. -/
theorem eq_completedEnvelopingMap
    {φ : CompletedEnveloping Ψ hΨ hΨs b →ₐ[R] CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a} (hφ : Continuous φ)
    (h : ∀ x, φ (toCompletedEnveloping Ψ hΨ hΨs b x) = toCompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a (g x)) :
    φ = completedEnvelopingMap g hg :=
  DFunLike.coe_injective (ModuleTower.eq_limQuotientsMap _ _ _ _ hφ fun x ↦ by
    have hx := h x
    rw [coe_toCompletedEnveloping, coe_toCompletedEnveloping] at hx
    exact hx)

/-- The identity extends to the identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem completedEnvelopingMap_id
    (h : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ m : ℕ, ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L m,
      AlgHom.id R UΦ (envelopingι cΦ a u) ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n) :
    completedEnvelopingMap (AlgHom.id R UΦ) h = AlgHom.id R (CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) :=
  (eq_completedEnvelopingMap _ h continuous_id fun _ ↦ rfl).symm

/-- The extension of a composite is the composite of the extensions. -/
theorem completedEnvelopingMap_comp (g' : UΦ →ₐ[R] CentralQuotient R (centralElement cΘ) c)
    (hg' : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ m : ℕ, ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L m,
      g' (envelopingι cΦ a u) ∈ orderLeftIdeal Θ hΘ hΘs c n)
    (hg'g : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ m : ℕ, ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L m,
      g'.comp g (envelopingι cΨ b u) ∈ orderLeftIdeal Θ hΘ hΘs c n) :
    completedEnvelopingMap (g'.comp g) hg'g =
      (completedEnvelopingMap g' hg').comp (completedEnvelopingMap g hg) :=
  (eq_completedEnvelopingMap _ hg'g
    ((continuous_completedEnvelopingMap g' hg').comp (continuous_completedEnvelopingMap g hg))
    fun x ↦ by simp).symm

/-- The extensions of two algebra morphisms `g` and `g'` with `g ∘ g' = id` satisfy the same
relation. -/
private theorem completedEnvelopingMap_comp_eq_id
    (g' : UΦ →ₐ[R] UΨ)
    (hg' : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ m : ℕ, ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L m,
      g' (envelopingι cΦ a u) ∈ orderLeftIdeal Ψ hΨ hΨs b n)
    (h : ∀ x, g (g' x) = x) :
    (completedEnvelopingMap g hg).comp (completedEnvelopingMap g' hg') =
      AlgHom.id R (CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) := by
  have hid : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ m : ℕ, ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L m,
      AlgHom.id R UΦ (envelopingι cΦ a u) ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n :=
    fun n ↦ ⟨n, fun _ hu ↦ envelopingι_mem_orderLeftIdeal hu⟩
  rw [← completedEnvelopingMap_id hid]
  exact eq_completedEnvelopingMap _ hid ((continuous_completedEnvelopingMap g hg).comp
    (continuous_completedEnvelopingMap g' hg')) fun x ↦ by simp [h]

/-- **Isomorphisms of completed enveloping algebras.** An algebra isomorphism `e` such that `e`
and `e⁻¹` are continuous for the topologies of the left ideals `I_N` extends to an algebra
isomorphism of the completions, which is a homeomorphism
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.continuous_completedEnvelopingEquiv`,
`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.continuous_completedEnvelopingEquiv_symm`). -/
def completedEnvelopingEquiv (e : UΨ ≃ₐ[R] UΦ)
    (he : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ m : ℕ, ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L m,
      e (envelopingι cΨ b u) ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n)
    (he' : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ m : ℕ, ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L m,
      e.symm (envelopingι cΦ a u) ∈ orderLeftIdeal Ψ hΨ hΨs b n) :
    CompletedEnveloping Ψ hΨ hΨs b ≃ₐ[R] CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a :=
  AlgEquiv.ofAlgHom (completedEnvelopingMap e.toAlgHom (by simpa using he))
    (completedEnvelopingMap e.symm.toAlgHom (by simpa using he'))
    (completedEnvelopingMap_comp_eq_id _ _ _ _ e.apply_symm_apply)
    (completedEnvelopingMap_comp_eq_id _ _ _ _ e.symm_apply_apply)

section Equiv

variable (e : CentralQuotient R (centralElement (twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Ψ hΨ hΨs)) b ≃ₐ[R]
    CentralQuotient R (centralElement (twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Φ hΦ hΦs)) a)
  (he : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ m : ℕ, ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L m,
    e (envelopingι (twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Ψ hΨ hΨs) b u) ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n)
  (he' : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ m : ℕ, ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L m,
    e.symm (envelopingι (twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Φ hΦ hΦs) a u) ∈ orderLeftIdeal Ψ hΨ hΨs b n)

/-- The extension of `e` is the extension `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.completedEnvelopingMap` of the
underlying algebra morphism of `e`. -/
theorem completedEnvelopingEquiv_toAlgHom :
    (completedEnvelopingEquiv e he he' : CompletedEnveloping Ψ hΨ hΨs b →ₐ[R]
      CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a) =
      completedEnvelopingMap (e : UΨ →ₐ[R] UΦ) (by simpa using he) :=
  AlgHom.ext fun _ ↦ rfl

/-- The inverse of the extension of `e` is the extension
`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.completedEnvelopingMap` of the underlying algebra morphism of `e⁻¹`. -/
theorem completedEnvelopingEquiv_symm_toAlgHom :
    ((completedEnvelopingEquiv e he he').symm : CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs a →ₐ[R]
      CompletedEnveloping Ψ hΨ hΨs b) =
      completedEnvelopingMap (e.symm : UΦ →ₐ[R] UΨ) (by simpa using he') :=
  AlgHom.ext fun _ ↦ rfl

/-- The extension of `e` to the completions extends `e`. -/
@[simp]
theorem completedEnvelopingEquiv_toLimQuotients (x : UΨ) :
    completedEnvelopingEquiv e he he'
        (ModuleTower.toLimQuotients _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Ψ hΨ hΨs b) x) =
      ModuleTower.toLimQuotients _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs a) (e x) :=
  completedEnvelopingMap_toLimQuotients e.toAlgHom (by simpa using he) x

/-- The inverse of the extension of `e` extends `e⁻¹`. -/
@[simp]
theorem completedEnvelopingEquiv_symm_toLimQuotients (x : UΦ) :
    (completedEnvelopingEquiv e he he').symm
        (ModuleTower.toLimQuotients _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs a) x) =
      ModuleTower.toLimQuotients _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Ψ hΨ hΨs b) (e.symm x) :=
  completedEnvelopingMap_toLimQuotients e.symm.toAlgHom (by simpa using he') x

theorem continuous_completedEnvelopingEquiv : Continuous (completedEnvelopingEquiv e he he') :=
  continuous_completedEnvelopingMap e.toAlgHom (by simpa using he)

theorem continuous_completedEnvelopingEquiv_symm :
    Continuous (completedEnvelopingEquiv e he he').symm :=
  continuous_completedEnvelopingMap e.symm.toAlgHom (by simpa using he')

/-- If `e` and `e⁻¹` carry the currents of order `n` into `I_n`, the extension of `e` carries the
kernel of the projection to `U / I_n` onto the kernel of the projection to `U / I_n`. -/
theorem completedEnvelopingEquiv_mem_completedOrderLeftIdeal_iff {n : ℕ}
    (hn : ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L n, e (envelopingι cΨ b u) ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n)
    (hn' : ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L n,
      e.symm (envelopingι cΦ a u) ∈ orderLeftIdeal Ψ hΨ hΨs b n)
    {x : CompletedEnveloping Ψ hΨ hΨs b} :
    completedEnvelopingEquiv e he he' x ∈ completedOrderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n ↔
      x ∈ completedOrderLeftIdeal Ψ hΨ hΨs b n := by
  refine ⟨fun hx ↦ ?_, completedEnvelopingMap_mem_completedOrderLeftIdeal e.toAlgHom
    (by simpa using he) (by simpa using hn)⟩
  rw [← (completedEnvelopingEquiv e he he').symm_apply_apply x]
  exact completedEnvelopingMap_mem_completedOrderLeftIdeal e.symm.toAlgHom (by simpa using he')
    (by simpa using hn') hx

end Equiv

end Map

/-! ### The completed level comparison -/

section Level

variable {Φ Ψ : LinearMap.BilinForm R L} (hΦ : Φ.lieInvariant L) (hΦs : Φ.IsSymm)
  (hΨ : Ψ.lieInvariant L) (hΨs : Ψ.IsSymm) {k : R}

local notation "cΦ" => twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Φ hΦ hΦs
local notation "cΨ" => twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Ψ hΨ hΨs

/-- The level comparison carries the currents of order `n` into `I_n`. -/
private theorem levelEnvelopingEquiv_envelopingι_mem (h : Ψ = k • Φ) (n : ℕ) :
    ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L n, levelEnvelopingEquiv hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h (envelopingι cΨ 1 u) ∈
      orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs k n :=
  fun _ hu ↦ by simpa using envelopingι_mem_orderLeftIdeal hu

/-- The inverse level comparison carries the currents of order `n` into `I_n`. -/
private theorem levelEnvelopingEquiv_symm_envelopingι_mem (h : Ψ = k • Φ) (n : ℕ) :
    ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L n,
      (levelEnvelopingEquiv hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h).symm (envelopingι cΦ k u) ∈
        orderLeftIdeal Ψ hΨ hΨs 1 n :=
  fun _ hu ↦ by simpa using envelopingι_mem_orderLeftIdeal hu

/-- **The completed level comparison.** If `Ψ = k • Φ`, the level comparison
`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.levelEnvelopingEquiv`, which is the identity on currents, extends to an
algebra isomorphism from the completion of the level-one enveloping algebra `U(ĝ_Ψ) / (ι K - 1)`
to the completion of `U(ĝ_Φ) / (ι K - k)`. It is a homeomorphism and matches the kernels of the
projections to the quotients `U / I_n`. This holds for every `k`, including `k = 0`. -/
def levelCompletedEnvelopingEquiv (h : Ψ = k • Φ) :
    CompletedEnveloping Ψ hΨ hΨs 1 ≃ₐ[R] CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs k :=
  completedEnvelopingEquiv (levelEnvelopingEquiv hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h)
    (fun n ↦ ⟨n, levelEnvelopingEquiv_envelopingι_mem hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h n⟩)
    (fun n ↦ ⟨n, levelEnvelopingEquiv_symm_envelopingι_mem hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h n⟩)

/-- The completed level comparison is the extension
`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.completedEnvelopingMap` of the level comparison. The continuity
hypothesis `hg` is an argument, so this is stated for `rw` rather than `simp`. -/
theorem levelCompletedEnvelopingEquiv_toAlgHom (h : Ψ = k • Φ)
    (hg : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ m : ℕ, ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L m,
      (levelEnvelopingEquiv hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h : CentralQuotient R (centralElement cΨ) 1 →ₐ[R]
        CentralQuotient R (centralElement cΦ) k) (envelopingι cΨ 1 u) ∈
          orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs k n) :
    (levelCompletedEnvelopingEquiv hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h : CompletedEnveloping Ψ hΨ hΨs 1 →ₐ[R]
      CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs k) = completedEnvelopingMap _ hg :=
  AlgHom.ext fun _ ↦ rfl

/-- The inverse completed level comparison is the extension
`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.completedEnvelopingMap` of the inverse level comparison. -/
theorem levelCompletedEnvelopingEquiv_symm_toAlgHom (h : Ψ = k • Φ)
    (hg : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ m : ℕ, ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L m,
      ((levelEnvelopingEquiv hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h).symm : CentralQuotient R (centralElement cΦ) k
        →ₐ[R] CentralQuotient R (centralElement cΨ) 1) (envelopingι cΦ k u) ∈
          orderLeftIdeal Ψ hΨ hΨs 1 n) :
    ((levelCompletedEnvelopingEquiv hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h).symm : CompletedEnveloping Φ hΦ hΦs k →ₐ[R]
      CompletedEnveloping Ψ hΨ hΨs 1) = completedEnvelopingMap _ hg :=
  AlgHom.ext fun _ ↦ rfl

/-- The completed level comparison extends the level comparison. -/
@[simp]
theorem levelCompletedEnvelopingEquiv_toLimQuotients (h : Ψ = k • Φ)
    (x : CentralQuotient R (centralElement cΨ) 1) :
    levelCompletedEnvelopingEquiv hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h
        (ModuleTower.toLimQuotients _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Ψ hΨ hΨs 1) x) =
      ModuleTower.toLimQuotients _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs k)
        (levelEnvelopingEquiv hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h x) :=
  completedEnvelopingEquiv_toLimQuotients _ _ _ x

/-- The inverse completed level comparison extends the inverse level comparison. -/
@[simp]
theorem levelCompletedEnvelopingEquiv_symm_toLimQuotients (h : Ψ = k • Φ)
    (x : CentralQuotient R (centralElement cΦ) k) :
    (levelCompletedEnvelopingEquiv hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h).symm
        (ModuleTower.toLimQuotients _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs k) x) =
      ModuleTower.toLimQuotients _ (orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone Ψ hΨ hΨs 1)
        ((levelEnvelopingEquiv hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h).symm x) :=
  completedEnvelopingEquiv_symm_toLimQuotients _ _ _ x

theorem continuous_levelCompletedEnvelopingEquiv (h : Ψ = k • Φ) :
    Continuous (levelCompletedEnvelopingEquiv hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h) :=
  continuous_completedEnvelopingEquiv _ _ _

theorem continuous_levelCompletedEnvelopingEquiv_symm (h : Ψ = k • Φ) :
    Continuous (levelCompletedEnvelopingEquiv hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h).symm :=
  continuous_completedEnvelopingEquiv_symm _ _ _

variable {hΨ hΨs} in
/-- **The completed level comparison matches the left ideals.** It carries the kernel of the
projection to `U / I_n` onto the kernel of the projection to `U / I_n`, for every `n`. -/
theorem levelCompletedEnvelopingEquiv_mem_completedOrderLeftIdeal_iff (h : Ψ = k • Φ) {n : ℕ}
    {x : CompletedEnveloping Ψ hΨ hΨs 1} :
    levelCompletedEnvelopingEquiv hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h x ∈ completedOrderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs k n ↔
      x ∈ completedOrderLeftIdeal Ψ hΨ hΨs 1 n :=
  completedEnvelopingEquiv_mem_completedOrderLeftIdeal_iff _ _ _
    (levelEnvelopingEquiv_envelopingι_mem hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h n)
    (levelEnvelopingEquiv_symm_envelopingι_mem hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h n)

end Level

end TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra
